{
 "comment": "Shared vectors. Each step advances the clock by dt ms, updates the persistent inputs (vbus_mv = PSU-side bus, default 12000; servo_mv = servo-side bus after the relay, absent/null = follows the relay: vbus_mv while the previous step ended ARMED, else 0; estop/btn/jumper default false), runs poll(), then feeds tx; 'out' is the hex of every byte the MCU sends in that step. The MCU boots LATCHED (reason 6), so every vector that needs a DISARMED start begins with the 3-step 'clear boot latch' preamble (button held exactly 500 ms). 'wrap_bits' (default 32) is the tick counter width the firmware's ticks_diff wraps at (RP2040 MicroPython: 30). 'portable' vectors use only serial input and time (plus the boot-latch button press) and are the minimum set for the real MCU (H3); FakeMcu replays every vector (tests/test_firmware_vectors.py).",
